                <pb facs="0476" n="374" xml:id="pg374"/>

                <head>Status of intergovernmental debts owed the United States by reason of the
                    First World War<anchor n="1" xml:id="ch8-f1"/>
                </head>
                <p>[For exchanges of correspondence in connection with amounts due the United States
                    under arrangements effected by the World War Foreign Debt Commission, see
                    Department of State, <hi rendition="#italic">Press Releases</hi>, as follows: <list>
                        <item>Belgium: June 22, 1935, p. 467; December 21, 1935, p. 547.</item>
                        <item>Czechoslovakia: June 15, 1935, p. 446; December 21, 1935, p.
                            541.</item>
                        <item>Estonia: June 15, 1935, p. 452.</item>
                        <item>Finland: June 15, 1935, p. 449; December 7, 1935, p. 502.</item>
                        <item>France: June 15, 1935, p. 453; December 21, 1935, p. 543.</item>
                        <item>Hungary: June 15, 1935, p. 459; December 21, 1935, p. 548.</item>
                        <item>Italy: June 15, 1935, p. 448; December 21, 1935, p. 550.</item>
                        <item>Latvia: June 15, 1935, p. 455; December 21, 1935, p. 551.</item>
                        <item>Lithuania: June 15, 1935, p. 457; December 14, 1935, p. 525.</item>
                        <item>Poland: June 15, 1935, p. 460; December 15, 1935, p. 545.</item>
                        <item>Rumania: June 15, 1935, p. 450; December 21, 1935, p. 553.</item>
                        <item>United Kingdom (Great Britain): June 8, 1935, p. 428; December 14,
                            1935, p. 523.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>The foregoing Department of State press releases, omitting the statements of
                    amounts due, are reprinted in the <hi rendition="#italic">Annual Report of the
                        Secretary of the Treasury</hi> …1935 (Washington, Government Printing
                    Office, 1936), page 269, and <hi rendition="#italic">Ibid.</hi>, 1936, page 228;
                    see also <hi rendition="#italic">Ibid.</hi>, pages 58 and 77, respectively,
                    “Obligations of foreign governments”.]</p>










